 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#your-next-moves-on-ai-maturity"&gt;Your Next Moves on AI Maturity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#frequently-asked-questions-about-ai-maturity"&gt;Frequently Asked Questions about AI Maturity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;What is AI maturity for go-to-market teams?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;AI maturity measures how consistently a go-to-market team turns AI into measurable business outcomes. For marketing, that means AI runs in documented workflows, draws on clean customer data, operates under human oversight, and ties to metrics like MQLs, customer acquisition cost (CAC), and revenue. Sales and service use the same definition with different workflows and metrics.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Maturity beats counting pilots because pilots measure activity and maturity measures repeatability. A team can run ten experiments and still sit at the bottom of the curve if none connect to the CRM, have an owner, or show a before-and-after result.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Marketing leads to other GTM functions, with &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/state-of-generative-ai"&gt;42% of marketers reporting advanced AI use&lt;/a&gt; (Established or Transformational), compared with 27% in sales and 23% in service. For those functions, see the &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/sales/sales-maturity-model"&gt;sales maturity model&lt;/a&gt; and the &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/service/customer-success-maturity-model"&gt;customer success maturity model&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;The Research Behind This Guide&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HubSpot’s 2026 State of AI in Marketing research:&lt;/strong&gt; 1,754 marketers across North America, Europe, Asia, Australia, and Latin America. Stages are respondent-rated, so they show how teams describe their own maturity, not an audit of results.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HubSpot’s cross-functional study:&lt;/strong&gt; 6,000+ professionals found that &lt;a href="https://offers.hubspot.com/state-of-ai"&gt;90% say their company uses AI and 6% rate it a “transformative” adopter&lt;/a&gt;. This is a different population than the marketing-only 98% and 10%, so don’t compare them directly.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;McKinsey’s 2026 State of AI survey:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.mckinsey.com/capabilities/quantumblack/our-insights/the-state-of-ai"&gt;1,719 participants in 97 countries&lt;/a&gt;, fielded May 4 to June 8, 2026, for an independent view of scaling and financial impact.&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The four stages come from HubSpot’s research. The six-dimension scoring later in this guide is an editorial framework, not an official HubSpot metric. Treat all benchmarks as directional.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;What are the AI maturity levels in marketing?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;An AI maturity model includes stages that run from experimentation to scaled activation.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hubfs/blogbot/ai-maturity-2-20261026-2727881.webp" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;" alt="AI maturity stages mapped to Loop Marketing"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The four AI maturity levels distinguish Early, Emerging, Established, and Transformational adoption patterns. A team can sit at different levels in different workflows, so score the workflow first.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Early:&lt;/strong&gt; AI use is individual and ad hoc. No shared prompts, documented strategy, or CRM connection. Governance is informal. Results are anecdotal (“it saves me time”).&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Emerging:&lt;/strong&gt; A few team-level use cases exist, each with an owner. Data access is partial, workflows run beside the core process, and measurement stops at time saved or output volume.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Established:&lt;/strong&gt; AI runs inside repeatable workflows across channels and uses connected customer data. A documented strategy and basic governance exist, agents handle defined multi-step tasks, and results are tracked against funnel metrics.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transformational:&lt;/strong&gt; Workflows were redesigned around AI. Agents work under human oversight, governance runs daily, and results are measured against holdouts or phased tests. Saved time goes toward strategy.&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The payoff at the top is measurable: &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/state-of-generative-ai"&gt;96% of Transformational adopters met or exceeded their MQL targets, and they were roughly 3.5x more likely to outperform CAC targets&lt;/a&gt;. Among all marketers surveyed, 72% said AI makes it easier to hit revenue and MQL targets, and about 65% said the same for CAC goals. These results are self-reported, so treat them as directional benchmarks.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;How These AI Maturity Levels Compare to Analyst Models&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Most AI maturity models agree that capability builds in stages. They differ in scope: the two best-known...

&lt;p&gt;Over the past few months, the HubSpot Blog team has been testing and comparing various AEO tools, including Scrunch vs. Semrush, and here’s the high-level takeaway if you’re trying to choose: Scrunch is a dedicated answer engine optimization (AEO) tool built to monitor how your brand shows up in AI answers, while Semrush folds AI visibility tracking into the SEO suite many teams already run.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Get Started with HubSpot's AEO Tool" height="58" width="335" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Which tool is best for your team depends on your needs. This guide compares Scrunch vs. Semrush across four criteria that make a great AEO tool: answer engine coverage, citation tracking and auditability, reporting and export, and integration and workflow. Each comparison closes with a neutral verdict on who the tool serves best, and the guide ends with a validation plan you can run during free trials before you commit.&lt;/p&gt; 
